From bed98400ee3f9ffefdfd68066496f343905e2859 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mik Lin <mik.lin@quantatw.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:24:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dbus-sensors: preserve state on external sensor threshold
 updates

Currently, sensor objects are recreated whenever a configuration
change is detected. This causes the 'assertedLog' state to be lost,
preventing proper de-assertion of events when readings return to normal.

This patch implements in-place threshold updates for external sensors:
Try to update thresholds in-place instead of destroying and recreating
the sensor object, so that assertedLog state
(and therefore correct de-assertion behavior) is preserved.
- Intercepts sensor destruction if the object already exists.
- Updates threshold values in-place while keeping the object alive.
- Preserves event log IDs to allow successful event resolution.

Note: adding this logic changed clang-format's line-wrapping decision
for the enclosing lambda, so this diff also includes a full
re-indentation of the lambda body with no functional change.

This modification is related to
https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/90129

